        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 18:33:50.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-12669 lov: wait for OST to reread cached EC stripe",
        "message": "LU-12669 lov: wait for OST to reread cached EC stripe\n\nThe EC recovery read of an encrypted file reads a surviving data\nstripe again as stored on the OST, where its pages are cached as\nclear text.  CIT_EC_RD runs with ci_ndelay set, so if that OST was\nreconnecting, the reread failed at once and the whole read would\nfail with -EIO, even though the data could be rebuilt once the OST\nwas back.\n\nWhen the reread fails while the OST import is reconnecting, restart\nthe IO as for a page that another reader is recovering, and wait for\nthe OST in vvp_io_ec_rd_iter_fini() once all pages of the recovery\ngroup are released, then rebuild the data again.  The wait can be\nkilled, and ends when the OST reconnects, is deactivated or the\nclient is evicted.  An error from a connected OST still fails the\nread as before.  Like a read of a file without parity, the read\nwaits for such an OST even if more parity could rebuild the stripe.\n\nAlso fix the comment in lov_ec_read_raw_stripe(), which now reads\ndata stripes as well as parity.\n\nAdd sanity-ec test_56b to restart the OST of the cached stripe\nduring the recovery read and check that the read returns the data.\n\nFixes: 743662647859 (\"LU-12669 ec: fix EC recovery read for encrypted files\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I3d626ccbc5a94e322e64dfda004981d42a3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
